   "date": "2015-03-03T18:10:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: Stan v2.6.1 tagged",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Bob, how do you build the parser now? Before in rstan, we had a bunch of things like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">compiler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>but now gm/ is gone and appears to be replaced by lang/ Is that all that needs to be switched?<br><br>Ben</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, March 3, 2015 at 12:44:59 PM UTC-5, Daniel Lee wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I forgot to add the release notes to that branch. I&#39;ll update the file in Stan, but it won&#39;t be tagged until the next release.<br><br><br></div>Daniel<br><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Mar 3, 2015 at 12:01 PM, Daniel Lee <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href rel=\"nofollow\" data-email-masked>bea...@alum.mit.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.6.1\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.6.1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473723934000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pOa4OEY49USQqfwzDQYIX\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.6.1</a><br></div>\r\n</blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
